& [Server]
  + separate no-argument stdio MCP server with one tool named manage_native_lifecycle_custody
  + one process-local async mutex owns exactly one valid Slice9 registry initialized empty at startup
  + no change to Slice8 tool discovery or behavior

& [Command]
  + strict tagged REGISTER carries one complete lifecycle request
  + strict tagged VALIDATE carries one compact Slice9 handle
  + strict tagged INSPECT carries no payload
  + complete arguments are bounded before typed decode and unknown fields refuse

& [Response]
  + exact profile operation status registry summary optional handle optional lifecycle response optional bounded fault and fixed nonclaims
  + REGISTER returns registered status handle and successor summary only after atomic successor installation
  + VALIDATE returns validated status exact Slice7 response and current summary without mutation
  + INSPECT returns inspected status and current summary without request bodies
  + any adapter refusal returns no handle or lifecycle response and leaves state unchanged

& [Concurrency]
  + commands serialize on one async mutex
  + duplicate equal concurrent REGISTER calls yield one registered result and one duplicate refusal
  + state poisoning serialization failure and invalid retained state fail closed

& [TruthAndError]
  + outer MCP is_error is true for adapter refusal and for inner lifecycle_refused or input_refused
  + outer validated status remains distinct from inner lifecycle outcome
  + registry coherence and digest identity confer no external authority

& [Bounds]
  + Slice9 eight-entry eight-megabyte-per-request sixty-four-megabyte-total limits remain authoritative
  + complete MCP argument limit is Slice7 input ceiling plus 65536 wrapper bytes
  + fault text is at most 512 Unicode scalar values and tool summary remains short

& [Acceptance]
  + direct and official-client register inspect validate restart and concurrency paths pass
  + compact validation equals direct Slice7 response for valid and refused inputs
  + malformed oversized unknown duplicate missing substituted and restart handles refuse without mutation
  + focused debug release lint format evidence and diff gates pass

& [NonGoals]
  + retained request readback persistence authentication authorization client isolation expiry eviction crash recovery provider model runner filesystem network signing admission installation deployment execution internal llama.cpp FPGA remote OneDrive EVO-X2 and Minecraft
